GUARDIANA for Windows\par
\par
GUARDIANA brings together the ZERO browser, which cuts tracking attempts in real time and shows you every advertising auction; monitoring of the whole computer, which shows which companies your PC connects to; and the Watch, which pauses your GUARDIANA calls if another program uses your microphone, camera or screen (turn it on in Communications \u8250? Settings). Everything happens on this PC: no account and no telemetry.\par
\par
What this installer will do\par
- Copy the program to \u8220?Program Files\\Guardiana\u8221? and the GUARDIANA ZERO browser to \u8220?Program Files\\Guardiana\\ZERO\u8221?. ZERO uses Microsoft Edge WebView2, which already comes with Windows.\par
- Register the \u8220?GUARDIANA\u8221? service, which starts with Windows.\par
- Add the \u8220?Guardiana\u8221? shortcut, which opens the panel, to the Start menu and the desktop.\par
- Make GUARDIANA this PC's DNS, over IPv6 too. It first keeps an exact copy of your setting; uninstalling leaves it exactly as it was.\par
- Create the Windows task \u8220?GUARDIANA\\Vigilante\u8221?, which checks every minute that GUARDIANA answers and, if it does not, gives the previous DNS back, so the PC is never left without internet.\par
- Add the program folder to the PATH, so \u8220?guardiana verify\u8221? works in any console, and register guardiana:// links to activate the licence from the email.\par
\par
What it will NOT do\par
- It does not read the content of what you send or receive: only the name of the service, the time and the device.\par
- It does not open any port to the network. Only Home Mode, when you turn it on, opens ports on the home Wi-Fi; turning it off closes them.\par
\par
After installing\par
When it finishes, the panel opens and within a minute you will see this PC's queries. To give the DNS back without uninstalling: panel, \u8220?Status\u8221?.\par
\par
Seven days with everything and no card. After that GUARDIANA keeps working for free, with the history of the last 24 hours; the VPN, Home Mode and the full history come with the Plus subscription. What was recorded stays on your disk, whether you pay or not. Terms: guardianagroup.com/en/terms.html \u183? Privacy: guardianagroup.com/en/privacy.html\par
